  "body": "## Result\n\nA scoped all-length exact query theorem for a persistent dirty connector when imposed source updates have a **known binary dependence matrix**. This changes the independence hypothesis of Ross Richardson's merged PR1780; sequential no-prewrite/no-late-write output deliveries, arbitrary dirty inputs, and every mandatory source update are retained.\n\nFor update prefixes s_i and query/correction parities q_i,t_j, the exact complete-query bill is\n\n```\n2 sum a_i + min [sum b_i(2-q_i) + sum d_j t_j]\n```\n\nsubject to `XOR q_i=0` and `XOR(q_i*s_i) XOR XOR(t_j*v_j)=0`. The proof covers arbitrary query multiplicities, not just paired-readout candidates. Two reads around a source query attain every feasible parity choice without requiring intermediate connector coherence. Independent updates recover PR1780's formula.\n\nThe source-bound PR1439/PR1780 four-request pilot reuses one update row. It needs **59 scalar XORs**, versus **63** for the strengthened best coherent schedule and **87** separately closed. All mutations, readouts and source calls are paid. Actual return-to-origin head steps are 1128/1176/1472; the declared unit local-backend totals are 1423/1491/1907. The correlated word attains the componentwise query minimum of 4B+8A+0D.\n\n**Limits:** this is an optimum in the explicitly indivisible call alphabet. Opening the pilot's maps gives a cheaper, checked 31-XOR direct-fusion program. No selected physical caller, recursive rank-profile gain, supplier admission, contracting recurrence, formal-kernel theorem, measured runtime improvement or new kappa is claimed.\n\n## Evidence and reproduction\n\nOnly `research/correlated-update-delivery/` is added, with README proof, complete SELECTION/TASK/SOURCES/VERIFY metadata, source-parsed fixture, certificate, primary optimizer, code-disjoint full-alphabet Dijkstra oracle and integrity checks.\n\n```\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python scripts/research_package.py --package research/correlated-update-delivery\n```\n\nObserved on CPython3.12.12, Darwin arm64:\n\n```\nPASS_CORRELATED_UPDATE_DELIVERY instances=300 pilot=59/63/87 direct_fusion=31 maps=4096 controls=11 no_new_kappa\nPASS_CORRELATED_UPDATE_PACKAGE controls=5 optimized_relocated_read_only\nPASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/correlated-update-delivery outcome=completed\n```\n\nThe 300 cases exhaust d=1,2, k<=4, every update-vector sequence and three tariffs including exact fractions. The independent oracle settles21070states and agrees with an additional exhaustive parity enumeration;72cases beat coherent pricing. Checks include4096arbitrary2x2 map triples, all19dirty basis columns of each literal pilot,384exhaustive scalar dirty executions,16independent-update predecessor specializations and24periodic fixtures. Controls reject dependence drift, missing/late/early operations, omitted restoration, false invoices, source/receipt corruption and occupied-output overwrites. Optimized relocated replay and canonical regenerated evidence pass. No hosted-CI result is claimed.\n\n## Provenance and overlap\n\nFresh base `e112d71c8d7bb32435debcc54df932593dd8223a`. Single chooser draw `829a355b1cafac3569bc060e0062cf20`, recursive-interfaces / persistent-boundary. The complete draw and declared changed scope are retained.\n\nCredit Ross Richardson PR1780 (`15a91b5d634023a3a14129cbb240854c4b188111`) and PR934/943; woklerx PR1439 (`3852c2d03044895cebdc9b31b0c7131a617774d2`) / PR1442 (`7c573bc769798ce4e336fd5be630060bd9d69a71`); Hanson Sun's observable-connector-repair (different two-B/future-prewrite contract). Exact live heads were rechecked and all three numbered predecessors are merged. Shared cached coverage was329openPRs includingdrafts and692discussions/comments/replies, with complete pagination at18:11\u201318:12UTC; targeted final queries and Discussion1776 found no overlapping successor, without treating no-match as novelty proof.\n\nClaim: #research-claim-and-completion-record\n\nPrepared for Adam Gall with substantial OpenAI Codex (GPT-6 Astra) assistance in derivation, implementation, exact checking and prose. Apache-2.0. The selected record, frozen packages, upstream sources and shared indices are unchanged.\n\n## Research claim and completion record\n\nStatus: completed. The claim record is preserved here so this PR is self-contained. Historical coordination links in the committed research metadata refer to this record; the separate coordination discussion is being removed.\n\nDONE / claim released \u2014 https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2060 . Full commit: 3555161e4f292b49622ee05cfb3fbbb34ddfbf75. Base e112d71c8d7bb32435debcc54df932593dd8223a; one chooser draw 829a355b1cafac3569bc060e0062cf20, recursive-interfaces / persistent-boundary. Package research/correlated-update-delivery/.\n\nChanged premise: source updates have a known binary dependence matrix, rather than PR1780 independent inputs. Sequential no-prewrite/no-late-write deliveries, arbitrary dirty connector and all imposed mutations are retained. Exact all-length query optimum follows from final parity/syndrome constraints, a lower bound permitting arbitrary multiplicities, and an attaining A,B,A,[B] word without intermediate coherence.\n\nSource-bound PR1439/1780 repeated-row pilot: 59 XORs versus best coherent 63 and closed 87, including all mutations/readouts/source calls. Declared head-step invoices: 1128/1176/1472. Direct fusion is only 31 XORs outside the indivisible alphabet: no unrestricted circuit, admitted supplier, recursive-profile or kappa claim.\n\nCPython 3.12.12 optimized focused and registered replay PASS: 300 cases agree with code-disjoint unrestricted-query Dijkstra and exhaustive parities; 72 strict coherence gains; 4096 map triples; 19 dirty basis columns/pilot; 384 scalar dirty executions; 11 semantic and 5 integrity/portability controls. Parent independently reviewed/replayed before publication; no hosted-CI, independent-human or formal-kernel review claim.\n\nReproduce: `uv run --python 3.12 --no-project python scripts/research_package.py --package research/correlated-update-delivery`.\n\nCredit Ross Richardson PR1780/934/943, woklerx PR1439/1442, and Hanson Sun observable-connector-repair; their scopes remain valid. Open blocker: a real admitted caller with these dependencies and complete routing/hosting/precision/lifetime tariffs. Full original scope/selection and pre-computation budget are retained in the package. Substantial OpenAI Codex (GPT-6 Astra) assistance for Adam Gall; Apache-2.0.\n",
